       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like it might be a typo.\n\n**Sertraline 1000 mg PO daily is 5 times the maximum recommended adult dose.** The usual range is 50\u2013200 mg/day. Doses this high are in overdose territory, with a risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures and QTc prolongation.\n\nMy guess is that **100 mg** once daily was intended, which is a standard dose. Could you tell me which of these you want?\n\n1. **Sertraline 100 mg PO once daily**\n2. **Another dose within 25\u2013200 mg/day.** If this is a new start, the usual first dose is 50 mg daily, or 25 mg for anxiety or panic disorders.\n3. **1000 mg as written.** If this is really intended, please say so and give the clinical reason. I'd also strongly recommend checking with pharmacy first.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order."
